#: src/configuration-settings.md:32
msgid "Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:34
msgid ""
"The default values for the build system's Makefile variables are mostly "
"defined in the `mk` directory—particularly in [`mk/config.mk`](#mkconfigmk). "
"Local changes from the default values, however, should be applied in the [`."
"config`](#config) file, or temporarily on the `make` [command line](#command-"
"line)."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:36
msgid ""
"The build system uses GNU Make and Cookbook to coordinate the build system "
"in order. The [build system reference](./build-system-reference.md#cookbook) "
"and [porting application guide](./porting-applications.md#cookbook) have "
"more information about Cookbook."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:38
msgid ""
"Three important Makefile variables of interest are `ARCH`, `CONFIG_NAME`, "
"and `BOARD`, as they specify the system to be built. These, and other "
"important environment variables, can be seen in the following table:"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:40
msgid "Variable"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:40
msgid "Definition"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:42
msgid "`ARCH`"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:42
msgid ""
"Specifies the [CPU architecture](#architecture-names) that the system is to "
"be built for. The default value is `x86_64`."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:43
msgid "`CONFIG_NAME`"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:43
msgid ""
"Determines the name of the filesystem configuration, and is normally used to "
"construct the `FILESYSTEM_CONFIG` name (the `desktop` variant is used by "
"default)."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:44
msgid "`BOARD`"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:44
msgid ""
"For [supported QEMU single board computers](https://www.qemu.org/docs/master/"
"system/targets.html) such as Raspberry Pi 3B+ (`raspi3bp`) that require "
"special configuration. Defaults to empty."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:45
msgid "`FILESYSTEM_CONFIG`"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:45
msgid ""
"Determines the filesystem configuration file location. See the [Filesystem "
"Configuration](#filesystem-configuration) section below. The default value "
"is `config/$ARCH/$BOARD/$CONFIG_NAME.toml` or `config/$ARCH/$CONFIG_NAME."
"toml` if `$BOARD` is empty, but this can be changed if the desired "
"configuration file is in a different location."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:46
msgid "`QEMU_MEM`"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:46
msgid "Sets the QEMU RAM memory quantity, e.g., `QEMU_MEM=2048`."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:47
msgid "`QEMU_SMP`"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:47
msgid "Sets the QEMU CPU core quantity, e.g.,  `QEMU_SMP=4`."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:48
msgid "`PREFIX_BINARY`"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:48
msgid ""
"If set to 0 (`PREFIX_BINARY=0`), the build system will build the Redox "
"toolchain from source and will not download the toolchain binaries from the "
"Redox build server."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:49
msgid "`PREFIX_USE_UPSTREAM_RUST_COMPILER`"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:49
msgid ""
"If set to 1 (`PREFIX_BINARY=1`) the build system will download the Rust "
"compiler from rustup (Rust upstream compiler binaries) instead of building "
"it (only used with `PREFIX_BINARY=0`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:50
msgid "`REPO_BINARY`"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:50
msgid ""
"If set to 1 (`REPO_BINARY=1`), the build system will download/install pre-"
"compiled packages from the Redox package server by default, rather than "
"build them from source (i.e., recipes)."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:51
msgid "`REPO_OFFLINE`"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:51
msgid ""
"Enable the offline mode of Cookbook where recipe sources will not be updated "
"and download the smallest amount of data from the Internet as possible."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:52
msgid "`REPO_NONSTOP`"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:52
msgid ""
"Enable the nonstop mode of Cookbook where recipe build failure will not stop "
"the compilation of other recipes."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:53
msgid "`FILESYSTEM_SIZE`"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:53
msgid ""
"The size in MB of the filesystem contained in the final Redox image. See the "
"[Filesystem Size](#filesystem-size) section before changing it."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:54
msgid "`REDOXFS_MKFS_FLAGS`"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:54
msgid ""
"Flags to the program that builds the Redox filesystem. The `--encrypt` "
"option enables disk encryption."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:55
msgid "`PODMAN_BUILD`"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:55
msgid ""
"If set to 0 (`PODMAN_BUILD?=0`), the build system will use the build "
"environment from your Linux distribution or Unix-like system instead of "
"Podman. See the [Native Build](./building-redox.md) page for more "
"information."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:56
msgid "`SCCACHE_BUILD`"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:56
msgid ""
"If set to 1 it will enable the [sccache](https://github.com/mozilla/sccache) "
"object cache for Native Build. See [sccache in Native Build](./advanced-"
"build.md#sccache) page for more information."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:57
msgid "`PODMAN_CACHE_PULL`"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:57
msgid ""
"If set to 1 will download the cached Podman container instead of creating "
"one from scratch, disable if the cached container is broken"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:58
msgid "`FSTOOLS_IN_PODMAN`"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:58
msgid ""
"If set to 1 (`FSTOOLS_IN_PODMAN=1`), the build system will build the "
"installer inside Podman to avoid FUSE in the host system. See the "
"[Installing without FUSE](./advanced-podman-build.md#installing-without-"
"fuse) page for more information."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:59
msgid "`FSTOOLS_NO_MOUNT`"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:59
msgid ""
"If set to 1 (`FSTOOLS_NO_MOUNT=1`), the installer will not use FUSE to "
"create images. See the [Installing without FUSE](./advanced-podman-build."
"md#installing-without-fuse) section for more information."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:60
msgid "`CONTAINERFILE`"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:60
msgid ""
"The Podman container configuration file. See the [Podman Build](./podman-"
"build.md) page for more information."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:61 src/configuration-settings.md:93
msgid "`COOKBOOK_MAKE_JOBS`"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:61
msgid ""
"The number of maximum CPU cores used when building recipes, default is using "
"all CPU cores from `nproc`."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:62 src/configuration-settings.md:92
msgid "`CI`"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:62
msgid ""
"If set to any value (`CI=1`), the build system will not activate TUI, and "
"parallel execution of the build step is disabled ."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:64
msgid ""
"The Redox image that is built is typically named `build/$ARCH/$CONFIG_NAME/"
"harddrive.img` or `build/$ARCH/$CONFIG/livedisk.iso`."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:66
msgid ".config"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:68
msgid ""
"The purpose of the `.config` file is to allow default configuration settings "
"to be changed without explicitly setting those changes in every `make` "
"command (or modifying the contents of the `mk` directory). The file is also "
"included in the `.gitignore` list to ensure it won't be committed by "
"accident."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:70
msgid ""
"To permanently override the settings in the [`mk/config.mk`](#mkconfigmk) "
"section, add a `.config` file to the `redox` base directory (i.e., where "
"`make` commands are run) and set the overriding values in that file."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:72
msgid ""
"For example, the following configuration specifies the `desktop-minimal` "
"image variant will be built for the `i586` CPU architecture. These settings "
"will be applied implicitly to all subsequent `make` commands:"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:79
msgid ""
"📝 **Note:** Comments are supported using the `#` character 📝 **Note:** Any "
"QEMU option can be inserted 📝 **Note:** if [`podman_bootstrap.sh`](./podman-"
"build.md#new-working-directory) was run previously, the `.config` file may "
"already exist. 💡 **Tip:** when adding environment variables in the `."
"config` file, don't forget the `?` symbol at the end of variable names. This "
"allows the variable to be overridden on the command line or in the "
"environment. In particular, `PODMAN_BUILD?=1` _must_ include the question "
"mark to function correctly."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:84
msgid "Cookbook Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:86
msgid ""
"Cookbook (the build system) has environment variables that can be tuned for "
"more customization. To set these environment variables, write `export "
"KEY=VALUE` to `.config`. Note that these are environment, not Makefile "
"variables, so the `export` keyword is necessary."
msgstr ""

