#: src/configuration-settings.md:106
msgid "`cookbook.toml`"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:108
msgid ""
"Cookbook also has a configuration file. This file is rarely used because `."
"config` should be sufficient. Any configuration in this file will override "
"configuration from `.config` or environment variables. The `cookbook.toml` "
"configuration below can be used as a template:"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:110
msgid ""
"The `cookbook.toml` file mainly configures Cookbook options (`[cook]`) and "
"mirrors (`[mirror]`). Mirrors are used to replace the main code and binary "
"source URLs used in Cookbook recipes, useful for a quick way to use "
"alternative sources when the main server is offline or slow."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:113
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"# These options have defaults set below\n"
"#[cook]\n"
"#jobs = <nproc>\n"
"#nonstop = false\n"
"#offline = false\n"
"#tui = true\n"
"#logs = true\n"
"#verbose = true\n"
"#web = false\n"
"#compressed = false\n"
"\n"
"[mirrors]\n"
"# The uncommented option below is the default if [mirrors] is not set\n"
"# see the list of GNU FTP mirrors at: https://www.gnu.org/prep/ftp.en.html\n"
"\"ftp.gnu.org/gnu\" = \"mirrors.ocf.berkeley.edu/gnu\"\n"
"# \"github.com/foo/bar\" = \"github.com/baz/bar\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuration-settings.md:132
msgid ""
"💡 **Tip:** Mirrors option can also be used to override [precompiled Redox "
"packages](#repo_binary) source URL."
msgstr ""

